.TH MSIP-DRIVE 1 "September 2026" "Peios" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
msip-drive \- drive an MSIP conversation non-interactively
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B msip-drive
.RB [ --socket " " PATH ]
.RB [ --kind " " NAME ]
.RB [ --set " " REF=VALUE ] ...
.RB [ --set-file " " REF=PATH ] ...
.RB [ --press " " REF ] ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B msip-drive
is a scriptable MSIP surface.  It prints every turn, supplies values to named
inputs, and consumes action references in command-line order.  It understands
the protocol rather than any particular installer flow.
.PP
Secret elements are masked in output.  Supplying a secret with
.B --set
can still expose it through the process argument list; use
.B --set-file
for credentials and other secrets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --socket " PATH"
Connect to PATH instead of
.IR /run/installerd.sock .
.TP
.BI --kind " NAME"
Start NAME instead of the
.B install
conversation.
.TP
.BI --set " REF=VALUE"
Provide VALUE when the named enabled input appears.  May be repeated.  VALUE
is visible in the process argument list and must not contain a secret.
.TP
.BI --set-file " REF=PATH"
Provide the exact UTF-8 contents of PATH when the named enabled input appears.
The value is read without placing it in the process argument list.  May be
repeated.
.TP
.BI --press " REF"
Press REF on the next actionable turn.  May be repeated; order is significant.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command help.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Show the program version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the conversation completed.  One means connection, protocol, or
flow failure; two means invalid command-line usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR installerd (8),
.BR install-tui (1),
.BR oobed (8)
